#
# Clean conformance fixture for math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape (Rule P3): a
# math:ProbabilityValue that names its gmeow:hasReferenceFrame, so the sh:or (reference
# frame OR probability model) is satisfied. Following the exact-rational discipline (AC#6)
# its exact magnitude 1/2 is carried as a math:RationalValue (also satisfying
# math:RationalValueShape); it is not typed math:OddsValue / math:LogOddsValue (P2) and
# carries no logic:confidence (P10). It MUST raise NO probability failure class.
# Positive counterpart of counter-examples/probability-value-unframed.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecProbabilityValueFramed).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:framedProbability a math:ProbabilityValue , math:RationalValue ;
    math:numerator 1 ;         # 1/2 = 0.5, within [0, 1]
    math:denominator 2 ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:fairCoinFrame .

ex:fairCoinFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .
<http://example.org/math/framedProbability> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
